## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION
None observed. Traffic flowed steadily throughout with no queues, jams or crowd build-ups recorded.

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
None observed. No wrong-way driving, helmetless riders, red-light jumping or illegal parking was recorded. (The red van at minute 42 and the "FS COURIERS & CARGO SERVICE" van at minute 85 were stationary but no violation is stated.)

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The scene was remarkably consistent across the full 171 minutes: a busy, well-lit nighttime intersection with continuous, free-flowing mixed traffic and no alerts. The single most dominant and recurring element was a white hatchback entering from the left and exiting right at approximately the 30-second mark of nearly every minute, so regular as to constitute the baseline rhythm of the footage; its plate was repeatedly auto-read (inconsistently) as "123456"/"1234"/"W12345"/"79", suggesting a recurring or possibly looping vehicle. Around this constant, the traffic mix — auto-rickshaws of many colours, sedans in white/black/red, red and blue buses, vans, and motorcycles in nearly every minute — stayed stable from start to finish, with no clear peak or lull; activity was uniformly busy, marginally lighter only in the earliest minutes (0–24, described as light-to-moderate). Wet road surfaces recurred in intermittent clusters (minutes 15–32, 50–51, 77–96, 106–120, 128–149, 155–169), indicating repeated rain episodes through the night, though weather was otherwise clear. Other recurring features: the "WESTBANK"/"West Bank" background sign, red buses, motorcycles stopping briefly near the centre or crossings before moving on, and occasional pedestrians at the zebra crossings. The only deviations from routine were isolated reversing manoeuvres (minutes 104, 136, 154), a black car with blue lights turning into a side street (minute 138), and one fully legible registration (MH02CJ1537, minute 106).

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
No distinct quiet periods were observed. The closest to quiet was the opening stretch, minutes 0–24, where traffic was described as light-to-moderate rather than busy; thereafter traffic was steady and continuous in every minute, with no stretch devoid of activity.
